  "question": {
    "text": "If \\(z_1\\) and \\(z_2\\) are two complex numbers satisfying the equation \\(\\left|\\frac{z_1+z_2}{z_1-z_2}\\right|=1\\), then \\(\\frac{z_1}{z_2}\\) may be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "eIQr5",
      "text": "real positive",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BcNBY",
      "text": "real negative",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "yKBH2",
      "text": "zero",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "WN3o3",
      "text": "purely imaginary",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint : \\(\\left|\\frac{z_1+z_2}{z_1-z_2}\\right|=1\\)\n\\(\\left|z_1 / z_2+1\\right|=\\left|z_1 / z_2-1\\right|\\)\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/7kA_PKtwY5dS9DzWJKbmF4Fhc-V99wO7SgcNwqIwOn8.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nDistance of \\(\\frac{z_1}{z_2}\\) from -1 and 1 are equal\nSo, locus of \\(\\frac{z_1}{z_2}\\) is perpendicular bisector of line joining \\((-1,0) ~\\&~(1,0)\\)\n\\(\\therefore \\frac{\\boldsymbol{z}_1}{\\mathbf{z}_2} \\Rightarrow\\) purely imaginary or 0",
    "image": null
  },
